## 3. Otherwise: write a Python source

Create `scraper/sources/{{ venue.id }}.py` and set the source to `{adapter: custom, module: {{ venue.id }}}`.
Subclass `BaseScraper` (`scraper/base.py`):

```python
class BaseScraper:
    def fetch(self) -> list[RawPage]            # network only: self.get_page(url, ext="html"|"json", params=...)
    def parse(self, pages) -> list[Screening]   # pure function of the pages — must work offline
    def enrich(self, screenings) -> None        # optional detail-page lookups (self.enrich_by_url)
    # self.venue (VenueConfig), self.tz (venue time zone), self.params (the venues.yaml source: keys)
```

Helpers in `scraper/normalize.py`: `to_local(dt, tz)`, `iso(dt, tz)`, `make_id(venue_id, start, title)`,
`clean_text`, `smart_title`, `normalize_format`, `language_from_text`, `end_from_runtime`, `nearest_date`.

